       "text": "I can't enter this order. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change my answer, because I can't verify the clinical rationale and 50 mg is still five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Doses that high risk profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. They can also cause prolonged vasodilation and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label:** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily, or a lower dose, right now.\n- **Add another agent:** If 10 mg isn't enough control, the usual step is to add a second drug, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, instead of going above the maximum.\n- **Get a formal override:** If you think there's a real reason to exceed the label, talk to pharmacy or the attending. Pharmacy can also review the order through your hospital's high-dose override process. That process happens outside this tool.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter 10 mg once daily or a different dose."
